GO HELL GO ENGLISH PATCH - LICENSE AGREEMENT
Version 0.0.1 beta

Please read this agreement before you install or use the Go Hell Go English
Patch (the "Patch"). By installing, copying or using the Patch, you agree to
these terms. If you do not agree, do not install or use it.


1. WHAT THE PATCH IS

The Patch is an unofficial, fan-made English translation for the Windows PC
version of goHELLgo Tsukiotoshiteko (ゴーヘルゴー つきおとしてこ). It replaces the
game's Japanese text and some text images with English while it is
installed. Uninstalling it removes it and brings back the Japanese game.


2. IT IS FREE

The Patch is 100% free and always will be. Nobody may sell it, charge for
it, put it behind a paywall, or bundle it with anything that is sold. If
you paid for the Patch, you were scammed: the official download is free on
the project's GitHub page.


3. YOU NEED A FULL COPY OF THE GAME

The Patch is not the game and does not contain it. It works only with a
full, legitimately purchased copy of the PC version of goHELLgo
Tsukiotoshiteko, already installed on your computer. It contains modified
copies of some of the game's text and image data, which are of no use
without the game. It does not unlock, bypass or remove anything in the
game. Please buy the game to support its creators.


4. THE TRANSLATION IS A MACHINE TRANSLATION

The English text is a machine translation. It has not been reviewed by
a professional translator. It may contain mistakes, awkward wording, wrong names, or lines
whose meaning differs from the original. The Japanese game is the
authoritative version of the story.

The translation follows the original script and is not censored. The game
contains crude humor, violence and other mature content, exactly as the
original does.


5. NO WARRANTY

THE PATCH IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,
FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, ACCURACY OF THE TRANSLATION, AND
NONINFRINGEMENT. YOU USE THE PATCH ENTIRELY AT YOUR OWN RISK.


6. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

IN NO EVENT SHALL THE AUTHORS, MAINTAINERS OR CONTRIBUTORS OF THE PATCH BE
LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER LIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF
CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE
PATCH OR THE USE OF IT. THIS INCLUDES, WITHOUT LIMITATION, LOST OR DAMAGED
SAVE DATA, A DAMAGED GAME INSTALLATION, AND ANY OTHER LOSS. Back up your
save data before you install the Patch.


7. NOT AFFILIATED WITH THE GAME'S CREATORS

The Patch is not made, endorsed or supported by Entergram or by any of the
game's developers or rights holders. All rights to the game, its story,
characters, art, music and original Japanese text belong to their
respective owners. Do not contact them for help with the Patch. If a rights
holder asks for the Patch to be taken down, it will be.


8. SHARING THE PATCH

You may share the unmodified installer with others for free, as long as
this agreement goes with it and you point people to the official project
page. Do not share modified versions as if they were the official Patch.


9. THE SOURCE CODE

The project's source code (the tools that build the Patch and the
installer script) may be used, studied, changed and shared
for non-commercial purposes, as long as this agreement is kept with it.
The source code contains no game files.


10. CORRECTIONS ARE WELCOME

The Patch is actively maintained. To suggest a correction, open a
"Translation fix request" on the project's GitHub page. Every request must
give:
  - the chapter where the line appears,
  - the line, copied exactly as it reads in the game,
  - the change you suggest, and
  - the reason for the change.
Requests without all four may be closed. By sending a correction, you agree
that it may be used in the Patch under this agreement, without payment.
The maintainer decides which corrections are made.


11. CHANGES TO THIS AGREEMENT

New versions of the Patch may come with an updated agreement. The
agreement included with your copy of the Patch is the one that applies to
that copy.
